  "dataset_summary": {
    "plain_description": "ModelOff 2016 Round 2 Section 2 'Fund the Future' competition problem. The workbook defines savings account projection assumptions for four investors (Alice, Bob, Charlie, Diana), each with an initial deposit, annual salary, salary growth rule, core deposit schedule, optional additional deposits, account close date, and investment return rule. A Formats sheet provides the workbook's cell-formatting legend. The logical schema normalizes the wide investor-by-assumption matrix into a dimension table (Investor), a long fact table of all assumptions (InvestorAssumption), a structured numeric/date sub-table (InvestorNumericAssumption), and a parameter table for the formatting legend (FormattingLegend).",
    "n_tables": 4,
    "notes": "T2 (InvestorAssumption) is the canonical long fact table derived from the wide D12:H19 matrix. T3 (InvestorNumericAssumption) surfaces only the two cleanly numeric columns (initial deposit, 2017 salary) and the single date column (account close date) that can be parsed unambiguously; the remaining assumption fields (salary growth rule, deposit schedule, investment return rule) are complex narrative strings retained in T2. T4 (FormattingLegend) captures the Formats sheet key-value legend which documents the visual conventions used throughout the workbook. Alice has no additional deposit; Bob has a one-off lump sum; Charlie and Diana have recurring deposit schedules. Investment return compounding frequencies differ across investors (annual vs. quarterly)."
  }
}